  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through Wednesday)\nIssued at 1247 PM CDT Thu Oct 29 2026\n\nA drier weekend is in store, before another mid to upper storm \nsystem early next week brings strong winds across the area. Highs \nSaturday rise into the 70s F, 80s F along the Rio Grande basin \nunder clearer skies and renewed light southerly winds. A low (less\nthan 30%) chance of showers/storms over the Marfa Plateau into \nLower Trans Pecos from daytime heating of elevated terrain is \nexpected afternoon/evening, with storms diminishing after sunset \nwhile lows fall into the mid 50s to mid 60s F range. A more \nprogressive weather pattern beginning late weekend Sunday brings \nanother round of higher rain chances (above 30%) Sunday for \nnorthern parts of the area, although the best forcing and \ntherefore heaviest rainfall are likely to remain to the north of \nthe area. Highs warm back into the mid 70s to mid 80s F by Sunday,\nwith warmer temperatures continuing through Monday. Winds shift \nfrom southerly to westerly from Sunday night through Monday \nmorning, with winds 35 mph or greater indicated for the \nGuadalupes/Delawares. These winds may persist through Tuesday, \nbefore cooler temperatures (upper 60s to lower 70s F highs, mid \n40s to mid 50s F lows) and lighter winds return to the area by the\nmiddle of next week.",
